ot evidence of variability unless the wavelengths are matched.","The flux scale is fitted on field stars (each above its local sky ring) outside a circle around the field centre that grows with the target's halo (up to 45% of the grid size); with fewer than 5 usable stars s = 1 and the difference also shows the wavelength change. A saturated target in a sparse field (e.g. R Draconis) often leaves too few stars and falls back to s = 1.","Saturated cores and detector defects carry no valid data (grey checkerboard).","Display only: the colour range is the field's brightest residuals or 10 x the noise (noise = robust sigma of the difference image). When the target region is much fainter (field range >= 2 x target-region range, e.g. WISE 0855), the range is set from the target region (its second-largest residual: one hot pixel cannot set it, and the brightest pixel there may clip) and brighter field-star residuals clip (saturate). Residuals under ~3 x the noise stay dark.","With two or three frames per season and detector, a faint target can stay in the noise: an empty target region at this depth is not evidence that the target did not move or vary."],"weights_definition":"Per coadd, 'weights' lists one weight per frame in the order of 'frame_ids': 1 / median VARIANCE of the frame's usable pixels, in (MJy/sr)^-2 (1 / robust noise^2 for a frame without a VARIANCE plane). Each pixel is the weighted mean of the frames valid there (sky removed per frame).","display":"Signed asinh: v = asinh(x / (softening x limit)) / asinh(1 / softening) for a residual x (MJy/sr) clipped at +/- limit ('limit_mjy_sr'). softening = min(1, max(0.05, 3 x noise / limit)) ('display_softening'), where noise is the robust sigma (1.4826 x median absolute deviation) of the difference image's valid pixels (not 'noise_mjy_sr', which comes from the propagated VARIANCE). 'field_limit_mjy_sr' = 99.9th percentile of the field's |residuals| or 10 x noise, whichever is larger. 'target_limit_mjy_sr' = second-largest |residual| within 'target_exclude_px' of the field centre (so one hot pixel or cosmic ray cannot set it; the brightest pixel there may clip), at least 10 x noise. 'limit_rule' is 'target_region' (limit = target limit) when the field limit is >= 2 x the target limit, else 'field' (limit = field limit).","colors":{"positive":"orange: brighter in the later season","negative":"cyan: brighter in the earlier season","no_data":"grey checkerboard: no valid data (off the cutout or saturated core)"},"coadds":[{"id":"D1_S0","detector":1,"season":0,"mjd_min":60790.26312899,"mjd_max":60790.26312899,"n_frames":1,"frame_ids":["2025W17_4B_0077_3D1"],"weights":[5367.699740837797],"skipped_frame_ids":[],"image":"compare/coadd_D1_S0.png","stretch":{"vmin":-0.21840912103652954,"vmax":4.368182420730591,"unit":"MJy/sr","method":"asinh"},"valid_fraction":0.9580320247933884,"core_pixels":12,"core_no_data_px":0,"core_fewer_frames_px":0},{"id":"D1_S1","detector":1,"season":1,"mjd_min":60961.975368689,"mjd_max":60968.086525796,"n_frames":2,"frame_ids":["2025W42_1A_0259_1D1","2025W43_1A_0019_1D1"],"weights":[5715.069096642954,5150.407103059067],"skipped_frame_ids":[],"image":"compare/coadd_D1_S1.png","stretch":{"vmin":-0.2192141538253054,"vmax":4.367377387941815,"unit":"MJy/sr","method":"asinh"},"valid_fraction":0.9962551652892562,"core_pixels":12,"core_no_data_px":0,"core_fewer_frames_px":0},{"id":"D1_S2","detector":1,"season":2,"mjd_min":61151.898093666,"mjd_max":61157.127646455,"n_frames":2,"frame_ids":["2026W17_1B_0351_1D1","2026W18_1A_0032_1D1"],"weights":[4501.557263493508,5688.704056328533],"skipped_frame_ids":[],"image":"compare/coadd_D1_S2.png","stretch":{"vmin":-0.21899203420616686,"vmax":4.3675995075609535,"unit":"MJy/sr","method":"asinh"},"valid_fraction":0.99974173553719,"core_pixels":12,"core_no_data_px":0,"core_fewer_frames_px":0},{"id":"D2_S0","detector":2,"season":0,"mjd_min":60799.703372034,"mjd_max":60799.704864303,"n_frames":2,"frame_ids":["2025W18_2B_0489_1D2","2025